But then, you know, when
you kind of pour into it

00:33:42.583 --> 00:33:45.350
and you see kind of a lot of
these women in prostitution

00:33:45.350 --> 00:33:48.680
were teenagers, they
weren't really consenting

00:33:48.680 --> 00:33:51.242
and the pimps get them drug
addicted and they beat them

00:33:51.242 --> 00:33:55.380
and, you know, so I thought,
hmm, maybe the state,

00:33:55.380 --> 00:33:57.500
the light touch of the
state has to kind of

00:33:57.500 --> 00:33:59.104
regulate some of that.

00:33:59.104 --> 00:34:00.350
And also these polygamist women,

00:34:00.350 --> 00:34:01.990
you know they were raised since the,

00:34:01.990 --> 00:34:05.543
you know the time they
were children this is

00:34:05.543 --> 00:34:06.540
what you're gonna do.

00:34:06.540 --> 00:34:07.558
You're gonna marry this old guy.

00:34:07.558 --> 00:34:08.391
Okay, what do they know?

00:34:08.391 --> 00:34:09.537
So then when you put
them on camera they go,

00:34:09.537 --> 00:34:12.061
"Yeah, yeah, I love being
a sister wife to so in so."

00:34:12.061 --> 00:34:15.400
But they don't really know
what the kind of autonomy

00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:17.610
and free choice would
be like if they weren't

00:34:17.610 --> 00:34:18.880
raised that way.

00:34:18.880 --> 00:34:20.880
To me this is a hard one
because it's implying

00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:23.220
that the state's gonna
get in there and muddle

00:34:23.220 --> 00:34:26.420
around about what it means
to have free will or consent

00:34:26.420 --> 00:34:27.516
or autonomy.

00:34:27.516 --> 00:34:30.370
- So this is, I don't
talk about it specifically

00:34:30.370 --> 00:34:32.160
in the book, but I did write a little bit,

00:34:32.160 --> 00:34:34.760
you know we had to cut some
things as you have to do.

00:34:34.760 --> 00:34:37.840
On the prostitution side
I'm actually okay with

00:34:37.840 --> 00:34:39.500
prostitution being legal.

00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:41.980
I get all of the more
traditional conservative

00:34:41.980 --> 00:34:43.110
arguments about what it does

00:34:43.110 --> 00:34:44.930
to the women and the family and all that.

00:34:44.930 --> 00:34:47.420
But we know it's
happening anyway and they,

00:34:47.420 --> 00:34:49.370
you know, there are plenty
of studies out of Amsterdam

00:34:49.370 --> 00:34:51.340
where they're in a union
and they get benefits

00:34:51.340 --> 00:34:53.140
and all sorts of stuff
and you can clean it up

00:34:53.140 --> 00:34:54.520
and get some of the drugs out.

00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:55.380
So that would be one.

00:34:55.380 --> 00:34:58.280
As for the multiple wives
I'm sort of with you.

00:34:58.280 --> 00:35:01.270
It's a messy one and
again this is where I get

00:35:01.270 --> 00:35:03.370
the more traditional conservative argument

00:35:03.370 --> 00:35:06.004
about the traditional
family as sort of the

00:35:06.004 --> 00:35:07.400
building block for everything else.

00:35:07.400 --> 00:35:09.790
So I would lean, I would lean against it

00:35:09.790 --> 00:35:12.621
just by saying if we're,

00:35:12.621 --> 00:35:13.830
if the government is involved in marriage,

00:35:13.830 --> 00:35:17.692
which it is right now then
it should just be one person

00:35:17.692 --> 00:35:20.493
can marry one person and
we just leave it at that.

00:35:21.653 --> 00:35:22.780
I think we should probably
put that one aside.

00:35:22.780 --> 00:35:23.860
That's a whole other thing.

00:35:23.860 --> 00:35:25.545
I know we've got one more here.

00:35:25.545 --> 00:35:29.940
- Okay, final point, so
one of my favorite books

00:35:29.940 --> 00:35:33.340
that gets pushed against me
I'm a big pro free speech

00:35:33.340 --> 00:35:37.450
idea and tolerance, is Carl
Poppers "Open Society."

00:35:37.450 --> 00:35:38.550
this is always thrown at me.

00:35:38.550 --> 00:35:40.083
What about the Poppers paradox,

00:35:40.083 --> 00:35:42.840
that is if you tolerate intolerant people

00:35:42.840 --> 00:35:44.050
the intolerant people will

00:35:44.050 --> 00:35:47.560
get power and they won't
tolerate you and therefore

00:35:47.560 --> 00:35:50.360
they'll get a toehold and then take over.

00:35:50.360 --> 00:35:51.862
What's your counter to that?

00:35:51.862 --> 00:35:56.100
- This is almost the
hardest one there is, right.

00:35:56.100 --> 00:35:57.560
That's why it's the paradox.

00:35:57.560 --> 00:35:59.910
And I think we see a
lot of this these days

00:35:59.910 --> 00:36:04.480
that there are a group of
highly intolerant people

00:36:04.480 --> 00:36:07.240
who are telling everyone else
that they're the intolerant

00:36:07.240 --> 00:36:10.590
people when we know that
the ones who are saying

00:36:10.590 --> 00:36:13.850
it would gladly use the state
to silence other people.

00:36:13.850 --> 00:36:16.870
So this is a massive problem.

00:36:16.870 --> 00:36:20.420
I would say look right now it's like Trump

00:36:20.420 --> 00:36:24.210
happens to be in power
and, you know, they can say

00:36:24.210 --> 00:36:25.960
that the conservatives
and the religious people

00:36:25.960 --> 00:36:28.910
are all intolerant, but
nobody's coming to knock

00:36:28.910 --> 00:36:30.316
on their door.

00:36:30.316 --> 00:36:32.340
You can tweet at Trump
all day long that he's

00:36:32.340 --> 00:36:34.080
Hitler and all the worst
things in the world,

00:36:34.080 --> 00:36:35.892
then the gestapo doesn't
show up at your door.

00:36:35.892 --> 00:36:38.850
You don't get pulled to the gulag, right.

00:36:38.850 --> 00:36:41.357
What I do fear though
is the counter to that

00:36:41.357 --> 00:36:44.550
which is imagine if we had
a really progressive or

00:36:44.550 --> 00:36:47.494
leftist president and
suddenly the same thoughts

00:36:47.494 --> 00:36:50.618
were being presented,
you know, if he tweeted,

00:36:50.618 --> 00:36:52.180
you know, let's say it was
President Elizabeth Warren

00:36:52.180 --> 00:36:53.950
and she tweeted out something and suddenly

00:36:53.950 --> 00:36:55.358
all of the conservative commentators

00:36:55.358 --> 00:36:57.980
were telling her she's
Hitler and just saying

00:36:57.980 --> 00:36:59.590
all the awful things that people say

00:36:59.590 --> 00:37:02.260
about Trump all the
time I'm fairly certain

00:37:02.260 --> 00:37:04.855
that the progressives would gladly use

00:37:04.855 --> 00:37:07.803
the power of the state to silence dissent.

00:37:08.749 --> 00:37:10.240
So I do think this is,
this is almost one of the

00:37:10.240 --> 00:37:12.590
biggest problems that we have
right now because there's

00:37:12.590 --> 00:37:14.840
an assymetry between,

00:37:14.840 --> 00:37:16.730
it's not just an
assymetry of power it's an

00:37:16.730 --> 00:37:20.860
assymetry of what type of
people want to use power.

00:37:20.860 --> 00:37:23.982
Lefties are generally saying
we want the state to do things.

00:37:23.982 --> 00:37:27.800
They believe the state
can do a lot of good.

00:37:27.800 --> 00:37:30.045
The more libertarian
minded of us it's not that

00:37:30.045 --> 00:37:31.690
we don't think the state could do good,

00:37:31.690 --> 00:37:34.210
but we're leery that the
state could do a lot of bad,

00:37:34.210 --> 00:37:36.066
so we don't want to give
it that kind of power.

00:37:36.066 --> 00:37:38.731
So this is why the paradox is the paradox.

00:37:38.731 --> 00:37:43.120
- Yeah, I also think it's
very unlikely to happen here.

00:37:43.120 --> 00:37:46.370
It doesn't happen in
most places historically,

00:37:46.370 --> 00:37:48.785
you know, people always
throw up Hitler and Stalin

00:37:48.785 --> 00:37:52.520
and Mao and I guess Kim Jung Un now.

00:37:52.520 --> 00:37:56.358
But there aren't many of
those examples historically

00:37:56.358 --> 00:37:58.850
since the rise of democracies.

00:37:58.850 --> 00:38:02.740
Most democracies can
tolerate some intolerance

00:38:02.740 --> 00:38:05.370
without intolerant people
taking over the press

00:38:05.370 --> 00:38:06.678
and so on.

00:38:06.678 --> 00:38:10.407
As much as Trump has been
hammered for himself hammering

00:38:10.407 --> 00:38:12.660
the New York Times for example,

00:38:12.660 --> 00:38:15.100
the failing New York Times,

00:38:15.100 --> 00:38:16.930
apparently The New York
Times subscription rates

00:38:16.930 --> 00:38:18.400
are highest they've ever been

00:38:18.400 --> 00:38:21.410
and you know they seem to
be thriving pretty well.

00:38:21.410 --> 00:38:24.960
So whatever he's doing is
not stopping the press.

00:38:24.960 --> 00:38:25.940
- Well that's what I always say.

00:38:25.940 --> 00:38:27.753
It's like everyone's actually,

00:38:29.193 --> 00:38:31.395
you may want Trump to
behave more presidential

00:38:31.395 --> 00:38:33.020
or more professionally,
whatever that means, but he

00:38:33.020 --> 00:38:34.607
attacks the press.

00:38:34.607 --> 00:38:35.623
The press attacks him.

00:38:35.623 --> 00:38:36.456
Nobody gets thrown in jail.

00:38:36.456 --> 00:38:38.390
Nobody's being dragged
off and the rest of it.

00:38:38.390 --> 00:38:40.122
Which reminds me of the
Colin Kaepernick thing,

00:38:40.122 --> 00:38:41.997
which I write about.

00:38:41.997 --> 00:38:44.060
Which is Kaepernick decided to kneel

00:38:44.060 --> 00:38:46.140
that means so he expressed himself.

00:38:46.140 --> 00:38:48.110
Trump is allowed to say
what he wants about it.

00:38:48.110 --> 00:38:49.740
He can't use the
government to stop the guy

00:38:49.740 --> 00:38:52.305
from doing anything, but
he's allowed to voice an

00:38:52.305 --> 00:38:53.301
opinion too.

00:38:53.301 --> 00:38:54.700
The owners of the team are allowed to say,

00:38:54.700 --> 00:38:56.790
well this is becoming too
much of a headache or not.

00:38:56.790 --> 00:38:58.330
And I don't want him there.

00:38:58.330 --> 00:38:59.650
The fans are allowed to say,

00:38:59.650 --> 00:39:01.669
well I'm gonna protest
and not buy tickets,

00:39:01.669 --> 00:39:03.410
or I'm not gonna buy jerseys.

00:39:03.410 --> 00:39:05.480
So ironically the whole
Kaepernick thing was

00:39:05.480 --> 00:39:07.600
framed to the world as if free speech

00:39:07.600 --> 00:39:10.400
was under attack, but literally everybody

00:39:10.400 --> 00:39:13.130
from the fans to the
president of the United States

00:39:13.130 --> 00:39:15.833
and everyone in between,
the owners, the whole thing,

00:39:16.891 --> 00:39:18.109
everyone expressed themselves.

00:39:18.109 --> 00:39:18.942
And nobody was dragged off.

00:39:18.942 --> 00:39:21.210
So this is where I think it
would probably be a good ending.

00:39:21.210 --> 00:39:23.774
It's sort of like this
is where America's done

00:39:23.774 --> 00:39:26.440
tolerance pretty well.

00:39:26.440 --> 00:39:28.290
And we should just be leery about throwing

00:39:28.290 --> 00:39:30.296
the baby out with the bathwater.

00:39:30.296 --> 00:39:32.620
- Well those were all the
right answers so I'm not

00:39:32.620 --> 00:39:34.734
gonna burn your book after all.

